Description: scProtXpress quantifies single-cell protein expression at the
    cell-type level by aligning samples to per-marker landmarks (ADTnorm-style
    negative / valley / positive peaks), discretising query cells against the
    bootstrap thresholds of a reference, and calling expression levels per
    population with a binomial test on the discretised matrix. The same
    pipeline handles CyTOF and CITE-seq scProtein inputs through a single
    `run_scProteinXpress()` entry point that dispatches modality-specific
    ingest while sharing every downstream step (QC, bootstrap, discretisation,
    signature frame, expression-level call).
